 "questions": [
  {
   "id": 242419,
   "is_answer_order_important": true,
   "stimulus_html": "<figure class=\"unnumbered\">\n<img src=\"exercises/media/458f8411310aee65.jpg\" alt=\"\">\n<figcaption>(credit: modification of work by John A. Vucetich/The Wolves and Moose of Isle Royale)</figcaption>\n</figure>\n",
   "stem_html": "<p>The graph shows the wolf and moose populations in Isle Royale, a protected national park in Michigan. Wolves are the main predator of moose, but there are many other factors at play.</p>\n<p>Around 1984, the moose population suddenly crashed.</p>\n<p>Make a hypothesis explaining why the wolf population did not increase during this time.</p>",
   "answers": [
    {
     "id": 759138,
     "content_html": "The moose population dropped due to a very severe winter."
    },
    {
     "id": 759137,
     "content_html": "The moose population dropped due to over hunting by the wolves."
    },
    {
     "id": 759136,
     "content_html": "The moose population dropped due to a disease slowly spreading through the population."
    },
    {
     "id": 759135,
     "content_html": "The moose population dropped due their habitat being destroyed by people."
    }
   ],
